old town · Kebaya, patterns, and Peranakan beauty through Chang Pong's brush</p><p class="story-meta">ปรับปรุงเมื่อ 
2026-09-09 · เวลาอ่าน 5 นาที</p></header><figure class="hero-photo-v2"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-09.webp" width="900" height="1092" alt="Peranakan Charm No. 9 · A woman in a blue, 
gold-embroidered kebaya with a kosang brooch and gold bracelet, among peonies and butterflies." 
loading="eager"><figcaption><span>Peranakan Charm No. 9 · A woman in a blue, gold-embroidered kebaya with a kosang 
brooch and gold bracelet, among peonies and butterflies.</span><span class="credit">Changpong · Tinnapop 
Ngansathir</span></figcaption></figure><div class="story-layout-v2"><div class="story-main-v2"><div 
class="story-lede-v2"><p>The first of the six A's in Takua Pa old town is open · Aphon invites us to read the town 
through clothing, patterns, and accessories in Chang Pong's paintings.</p><p>Peranakan Charm is shown in September 
2026 at 78 Studio on Takua Pa Culture Street. This story follows the project information and what is visible in the 
paintings; unverified history is marked clearly.</p></div><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 id="section-0">The six 
A's are a way to read the town</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" 
width="1000" height="1000" alt="Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>Takua Pa Old Town 
Cultural Street</span><span class="credit">Illustration</span></figcaption></figure><p>Kuapapoh presents six A's: 
Aphon, Asai, Ahan, Arom, Aram, and Akhan. They cover local clothing, ways of living, food, art and music, temples and 
shrines, and buildings and architecture.</p><p>Aphon opened first because the exhibition at 78 Studio gives us 
something to see immediately in September 2026 · clothing becomes the first doorway into the town's beauty and 
identity.</p></section><blockquote class="pull-quote-v2"><p>Peranakan Charm is evidence of identity across every stage 
of a life shaped by a love of art amid Peranakan culture.</p></blockquote><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 
id="section-1">Peranakan clothing in the paintings</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-kebaya-pink.webp" width="900" height="1142" alt="A woman in a pink 
floral-embroidered kebaya, wearing three gold kosang brooches, against a blue background with roses." 
loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>A woman in a pink floral-embroidered kebaya, wearing three gold kosang brooches, 
against a blue background with roses.</span><span class="credit">Changpong · Tinnapop 
Ngansathir</span></figcaption></figure><p>The paintings show kebaya, a blue gold-embroidered kebaya, white cutwork 
lace, floral batik, kosang brooches, gold bracelets, and a lacquered tiffin carrier. These details appear together 
with color, flowers, backgrounds, and the women's poses.</p><p>The project describes Aphon as local clothing, lace, 
batik sarongs, textile patterns, and accessories. Chang Pong's paintings make that description visible.</p><p>The 
academic reason why a town shaped by mining has these clothes is not verified in the sources used here · what can be 
stated is that the project connects clothing with the town's story, while the artist conveys it through color, 
pattern, and dress.</p><div class="story-flags-v2"><span class="story-flag-v2 flag-unverified">The clothing's 
historical background is not verified</span></div></section><section class="story-section-v2"><h2 
id="section-2">Peranakan Charm at 78 Studio</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-expo-corner.webp" width="1400" height="1050" alt="The first corner of the exhibition at 
78 Studio, with the artist biography on an easel and works hung on an old wooden shelf." 
loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>The first corner of the exhibition at 78 Studio, with the artist biography on an 
easel and works hung on an old wooden shelf.</span><span class="credit">Kuapapoh project · Ji Show 
Muang</span></figcaption></figure><p>The solo exhibition Peranakan Charm by Chang Pong · Tinnapop Ngansathin runs in 
September 2026 at 78 Studio on Takua Pa Culture Street. It uses brushwork to tell the town's story through pattern, 
color, and clothing, linking past and 
present.</p><p>โครงการกั่วป่าโพ้ฟื้นพื้นที่ว่างในอาคารเก่าให้เป็นพื้นที่สร้างสรรค์ บ้านเลขที่ 78 
เดิมเป็นบ้านนายเหมืองและบริษัทเหมืองแร่ดีบุก ปัจจุบันเป็นกั่วป่าเหมืองมิวเซียมที่มีกิจกรรมหมุนเวียน · 
อ่านรายละเอียดของพื้นที่และโครงการได้ที่ <a href="https://kuapapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" 
rel="noopener">เว็บไซต์กั่วป่าโพ้</a></p><p>Chang Pong was born in Takua Pa old market. He studied at Silpakorn 
University, has exhibited his art, illustrated buildings and places in Phang Nga, worked on the film RAMBO 6, and 
makes book covers. He is now an assistant municipal artist and an independent artist.</p></section><section 
class="story-section-v2"><h2 id="section-3">Where to see it</h2><figure class="section-photo-v2"><img 
src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" width="1000" height="667" alt="Tao Ming School" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>Tao Ming 
School</span><span class="credit">Illustration</span></figcaption></figure><p>Peranakan Charm is open every day at 78 
Studio on Takua Pa Culture Street in September 2026. The project also lists house 109 as open Sundays and house 305 as 
open every Sunday.</p><p>ก่อนออกเดินทาง คุณตรวจสอบข่าวการจัดแสดงและรายละเอียดล่าสุดได้ที่ <a 
href="https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61590430773715" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เพจกั่วป่าโพ้</a> 
และติดตามภาพรวมโครงการได้ที่ <a href="https://kuapapoh.pages.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">กั่วป่าโพ้ · 
จีโชว์เมือง</a></p></section><section class="story-places-v2"><h2>Where to visit in person</h2><div 
class="mini-cards-v2"><div class="place-card-mini"><div><h3>Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</h3><button 
class="button button-outline" data-trip-add="culture-street">Add to trip</button></div></div><div 
class="place-card-mini"><div><h3>Tao Ming School</h3><button class="button button-outline" 
data-trip-add="tao-ming">Add to trip</button></div></div></div></section><section 
class="story-gallery-v2"><h2>Gallery</h2><section class="story-gallery-group"><h3>Clothing works</h3><div 
class="story-gallery-grid"><figure class="story-gallery-card"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-kebaya-green.webp" alt="A braided woman in a sea-green kebaya embroidered with 
roses, set against golden yellow and peonies." loading="lazy" width="900" height="1121"><figcaption><span>A braided 
woman in a sea-green kebaya embroidered with roses, set against golden yellow and peonies.</span><span 
class="credit">Changpong · Tinnapop Ngansathir</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="story-gallery-card"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-lace-white.webp" alt="A woman in a white cutwork lace blouse and floral batik 
sarong, holding a lacquered tiffin carrier, against emerald batik." loading="lazy" width="900" 
height="908"><figcaption><span>A woman in a white cutwork lace blouse and floral batik sarong, holding a lacquered 
tiffin carrier, against emerald batik.</span><span class="credit">Changpong · Tinnapop 
Ngansathir</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="story-gallery-card"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-charm-09-wall.webp" alt="Peranakan Charm No. 9 hanging on a wooden shelf in the 
exhibition, with a label showing the work’s dimensions." loading="lazy" width="1050" 
height="1400"><figcaption><span>Peranakan Charm No. 9 hanging on a wooden shelf in the exhibition, with a label 
showing the work’s dimensions.</span><span class="credit">Kuapapoh project · Ji Show 
Muang</span></figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="story-gallery-group"><h3>Exhibition and artist 
views</h3><div class="story-gallery-grid"><figure class="story-gallery-card"><img 
src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-expo-wall.webp" alt="A wall of large works along the exhibition walkway." loading="lazy" 
width="1050" height="1400"><figcaption><span>A wall of large works along the exhibition walkway.</span><span 
